…"],["2c2b8313_0d68de69",3,-8,1,"nit: It doesn't *really* matter because `BOOL` and `bool` are largely interchangeable, but for consistency, let's use `false` here (and `true`) below, to match the type (`std::optional<bool>`) of the…"],["e4c61618_d20363da",4,-8,0,"With the other changes you've made, I don't think it's necessary to implement your own getter/setter anymore. You can delete these."],["27efd6a6_857a7d31",4,-6,1,"`std::optional<bool>` are difficult to use, because they are implicitly convertible to `bool`. I would suggest using an enum instead. ``` class enum VoiceOverOverrideForTesting { kNotOverridden,…"],["b739eea2_b37d0a3f",61,-6,1,"Following my other recommendation, change this to a pair of methods: ``` - (void)setOverrideVoiceOverForTesting:(BOOL)value; - (void)clearOverrideVoiceOverForTesting; ```"]],0,67],[7128044,20404,3,0.147,0.096,[[0,40]],[["2000b1db_72822c7d",62,-1,1,"Let's remove this block and do, I think it should work. `base::test::ScopedFeatureList feature_list_{autofill::features::kAutofillEnableCvcStorageAndFilling};`"]],0,68],[7063349,20410,40,1.341,1.058,[[10,0.587,6,24],[1,0.304,33,12],[7,0.109,11,4]],[["ea53f2d4_3c0016f4",63,-6,1,"Back to previous line."],["73fed360_d79c3261",63,-5,1,"It's not a requirement - the users can opt-in to use re-auth, which will always authenticate them. Please refer to previous re-auth flag descriptions and word this similarly"],["5912995c_d1044d98",64,-4,1,"Please also add the comment above this for what this feature does"]],0,69],[7065431,20411,68,4.226,3.283,[[1,34]],[["23c9c4a4_b2dc61b2",65,-7,1,"Put this in the elif block itself instead of nesting in the existing one."],["d0ff54ff_7b9db770",65,-7,1,"Same here and below."],["9331b726_675728cd",65,-1,1,"nit: Remove for consistency with the existing #elif in the file? Same elsewhere. I don't know what the convention is (`git cl format` doesn't autogenerate those comments) but the comments make little…"]],0,70],[7165135,20411,1,0.147,0.096,[[0,41]],[],